# Ctrl+F and the EXPERIMENTAL tab: Mission Planner's temp form (the owner's request of
# 2026-10-04).
#
# Mission Planner's Ctrl+F is MainV2.ProcessCmdKey's `new temp().Show()` (MainV2.cs:4099-4105),
# the welcome text's "Control-F - Temp screen". Here, by the owner's word, it is the EXPERIMENTAL
# tab between LOGS and PLUGINS, and Ctrl+F shows it: temp.cs's table of 63 buttons, each beside
# what it does, as temp.Designer.cs and temp.resx lay them out (crates/mp-gui/src/experimental.rs).
#
# The claim: Ctrl+F shows the tab; the 63 buttons are there, sixteen working - nine opening
# windows this application has, seven tools of its own (experimental-actions.gui); NMEA opens
# the NMEA output window as CONFIG > Advanced's NMEA does; a ruled-out tool says why on the status
# line, and one not yet ported says so.
screen fly
# Smaller than the owner's Mac window, where rows ran off the bottom (2026-10-04): the run's
# end checks the table is wholly on screen (layout_guard's EXPERIMENTAL entry).
window 1280x800
budget 12
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
setup printf '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Config><tabcontrolactions>tabQuick;</tabcontrolactions></Config>' > "$WORK/config.xml"
expect screen fly
key ctrl+f
expect screen experimental
expect experimental.buttons 63
expect experimental.working 20
# A window this application has: the NMEA output, as Advanced's NMEA opens it.
click experimental-BUT_outputnmea
expect experimental.last BUT_outputnmea
expect config.nmea.window true
click nmea-close
expect config.nmea.window false
# Out of scope by a ruling: Swarm says so, and why.
click experimental-BUT_swarm
expect experimental.last BUT_swarm
expect status ~ Swarm: out of scope, the owner's ruling (PLAN.md section 12 D13
# Not ported yet: structtest says so.
click experimental-but_structtest
expect status ~ structtest: not ported yet
# The tab itself, from another screen.
click tab-fly
expect screen fly
click tab-experimental
expect screen experimental
